  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the priority is to establish a simple, low-cost reference point before testing more complex profile, encoder, or fusion choices. config_001 is the minimal RNA-only single-profile PCA baseline, so it isolates basic RNA representation without aggregation or multimodal fusion. Its result will calibrate later comparisons: if it performs well, it becomes a strong anchor for testing learned RNA encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, and fusion; if it underperforms, it motivates shifting budget toward image-only or multimodal configurations. This is the best first experiment because it reduces uncertainty with minimal confounds and avoids prematurely committing to a more complex design."
